File: nix/agda-algebras-4662373d-stdlib-2.4.patch

agda-algebras at 4662373d (the benchmark and corpus commit, issue #127),
moved to standard-library 2.4.1 under the released Agda 2.9.0 (issue #374).
flake.nix applies it in mkAgdaAlgebrasPkg; nothing else reads it.

+  agda-algebras.agda-lib: `depend: standard-library-2.3` becomes `-2.4`,
   the library name of 2.4.1, which the old line does not match.
+  src/: five names standard-library 2.4 deprecates become the
   replacements its WARNING_ON_USAGE pragmas name, each defined as an
   alias of the replacement, with the same fixity:
     _×-dec_ to _×?_, _→-dec_ to _→?_, _⊎-dec_ to _⊎?_
       (Relation.Nullary.Decidable.Core),
     ¬∀⟶∃¬ to ¬∀⇒∃¬, ¬∀⟶∃¬-smallest to ¬∀⇒∃¬-smallest (Data.Fin.Properties).
   144 replacements in 23 modules: 104 uses (the 104 warnings the release
   raised without this patch), 39 import entries, and one prose mention.
   The same renames agda-algebras made upstream in ualib/agda-algebras
   PR #642.

Made by a token-aware replacement over a checkout of 4662373d, then
`git diff`; the text above the first `diff` line is ignored by patch.

